cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this experimental release and the upstream work credited in README.md."
title: "Smaller ZF proof-search Turing machines"
type: software
authors:
  - name: aimir
    website: "https://github.com/aimir"
repository-code: "https://github.com/aimir/tiny-zf"
url: "https://github.com/aimir/tiny-zf/releases/tag/v0.2.0-experimental"
version: "0.2.0-experimental"
date-released: 2026-10-13
abstract: >-
  Reproducible experiments producing a 308-state proof-search Turing machine
  using a corrected ICS formulation and Wade's compiler. Lean proves exact
  blank-tape halting equivalence with the independently defined numeric source
  calculus. The source theory’s connection to conventional ZF remains unproved;
  this is not a verified ZF-independence result.
